git-khronos (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reload the window when its page renderer crashes on Linux instead of
    leaving a blank, unreachable instance.
  * Prevent a startup crash on the affected WSLg X11 path by using the
    current session's accessibility bus without disabling accessibility.
  * Show additions and deletions for unstaged changes, and give Unstaged
    Files more room when Staged Files is collapsed.
  * Review and discard all eligible unstaged files from one action. Support
    recovery for ordinary nested files on Linux without unstaging changes.
  * Offer to open the linked worktree that owns a checked-out branch
    instead of detaching the current checkout.
  * Add manual update checks and optional automatic updates with publisher
    verification. Automatic updates are off by default.
  * Copy the full commit ID from a file history row and clear clipboard
    feedback when the file history revision changes.
  * Keep large diff minimaps lightweight without changing where their
    jump buttons navigate.
  * Show invalid blame line numbers beside the input instead of offering
    to retry the last read.
  * Copy the full Git ref from branch and tag menus, even when the short
    names are ambiguous.

 -- Maurizio Casciano <mauriziocasciano7@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:38:17 +0100

git-khronos (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename remotes, local and remote branches, and tags.
  * Open the repository in the system terminal and resize the terminal panel.
  * Add a guided dialog to merge, rebase or fast-forward with a preview.
  * Load more dialogs on demand to keep startup lean.

